12408	{"artifactId":"LLD-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s3","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s3-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:01:03.608Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every s3 acceptance criterion (ac1–ac7) and the lc1 stakeholder policy in the DEF is designed; no non-goal (stage change, config read) is built.","evidence":"DEF-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c s3 lists ac1–ac7 plus lc1 ('a pending artifact superseded by downstream approval ... stops counting toward Needs attention'). The LLD covers approval states (ac1), approved-build-with-failed-task conflict while the stage stays complete (ac2), unrecorded tasks (ac3), unplanned tasks (ac4), unapproved block → review-blocked with the stage kept (ac5), approved or overridden block → not blocking but still shown (ac6), and the superseded-pending rule with attentionRule (ac7, lc1 recorded as confirmed 2026-10-08). The FR's 'unresolved references' come from s1 notices (sc3 'unresolved-parent' is attention true), which s5 joins in. Nothing here changes a stage. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The ArtifactGate/ItemGates shapes match the HLD sc5 interface sketch, and the departures from it are stated as stakeholder-confirmed readings.","evidence":"The HLD sc5 interfaceSketch has the same ArtifactGate fields, the same TaskValidation, ItemGates (storyLevelResult, conflict {failedTaskItemIds, storyLevelFailed}, attentionReasons, attentionRule) and GatePassResult maps. The sketch says effectiveVerdict is 'otherwise the recorded verdict' and that blocking means 'artifact unapproved'. The LLD refines both: a fully resolved block reads 'pass', and a CR's guarded gate is its story's BUILD. Both are called out in its 2.2 postconditions as readings confirmed on 2026-10-08. [files: .insrc/artifacts/HLD-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"effectiveReviewVerdict returns 'block' whenever any HIGH/MED finding has no resolution entry, regardless of the recorded verdict, and the approval gate uses exactly that, so a recorded 'warn' carrying an unresolved MED is effectively a block.","evidence":"resolve.ts:57-64 checks `report.findings.some(f => BLOCKING.has(f.severity) && res[f.claimId] === undefined)` and returns 'block' or 'pass'. gates.ts:581 refuses approval when `effectiveReviewVerdict(review, artifact.meta.reviewResolutions) === 'block'`. verdict.ts:44-50 computeVerdict gives 'warn' for a MED that blockOn excluded. A template review's could-not-verify finding is LOW (severityForOutcome), so it never blocks. [files: src/workflow/review/resolve.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/review/verdict.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"reviewerPartyOf reads reviewedBy first, then the model label ('client' → controller, any other label → daemon, none → unknown).","evidence":"party.ts:63-71 matches this. The live CR-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s2 meta carries reviewedBy 'daemon' and model 'claude:opus', so passing the CR's meta works. [files: src/workflow/review/party.ts, .insrc/artifacts/CR-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s2.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"codeReview.enforce defaults off, and code-review/gate.ts then demotes a CR block to an advisory warn, so CR blocking is an attention signal, not the enforced gate.","evidence":"code-review/gate.ts:102-112: when enforce is false it returns `{ status: 'warn', advisory: true, ... }`. readEnforceFlag (gate.ts:144-151) returns false when the config file or the key is missing. [files: src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ArtifactRecord.approval already gives state approved/rejected/pending with approvedAt/rejectedAt, and approved wins over rejected.","evidence":"load.ts:66-72 sets state 'approved' when approvedAt is set or status is 'approved', else 'rejected' when rejectedAt is set or status is 'rejected', else 'pending'. types.ts:33-37 carries approvedAt and rejectedAt, both nullable. An AMD approved only through status has approvedAt null, which the `at: string | null` type allows. [files: src/workflow/delivery/load.ts, src/workflow/delivery/types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"taskIdToOrdinal and storyIdToOrdinal throw on unparseable ids; graph.ts already wraps them in null-returning helpers; and their patterns do not overlap, so a 't3' entry can never be read as a story-level result.","evidence":"id.ts:119-126: storyIdToOrdinal matches /^[sS](\\d+)$/ and throws otherwise. id.ts:132-136: taskIdToOrdinal matches /^t(\\d+)$/ and throws otherwise. graph.ts:99-113 defines the storyOrdinalOf and taskOrdinalOf try/catch wrappers, but they are module-private (not exported), so gate.ts needs its own copies, as the LLD says. [files: src/workflow/id.ts, src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The sc5 types and gate.ts are new; ReviewVerdict is reused from review/types.ts; makeNotice/sortNotices and the 'unplanned-task' / 'validation-conflict' notice codes already exist with the stated attention values.","evidence":"The delivery directory has no gate.ts and types.ts has no ArtifactGate. review/types.ts:43 has `export type ReviewVerdict = 'pass' | 'warn' | 'block'`, and code-review/gate.ts:32 already imports it as a type. types.ts:120-121 includes the 'unplanned-task' and 'validation-conflict' NoticeCodes. notice.ts:17-30 sets 'validation-conflict': true and 'unplanned-task': false, and makeNotice (notice.ts:44) takes `{ itemIds, artifactIds }` refs. [files: src/workflow/delivery/types.ts, src/workflow/delivery/notice.ts, src/workflow/review/types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The sc2 fields the pass consumes (evidenceArtifactIds, childIds, sourceIds, plannedTaskIds) exist. Task items are minted only from t<n> ids, and a story-id BUILD entry is left as no task item, so storyLevelResult can be derived without colliding with a task.","evidence":"types.ts:77-98 WorkItemNode has sourceIds, childIds, evidenceArtifactIds and plannedTaskIds. graph.ts:381-398 addTasks skips any entry where `taskOrdinalOf(taskId) === null`, so 'S001' becomes no task. Live BUILD-0855311b6b32eb72-s1 has its only entry as `id: \"S001\", passed: false` with approvedAt set, and fixtures.ts:150 already includes it. [files: src/workflow/delivery/types.ts, src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts, src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/fixtures.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A CR record lands in its story's evidence (it carries meta.epicHash and meta.storyId), so the CR's 'guarded gate' (the story's BUILD) can be found among the same item's records.","evidence":"CR-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s2.json meta has epicHash '2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c' and storyId 's2'. graph.ts groupKeyOf (lines 43-51) keys records by hash and story ordinal, so the CR and the BUILD of the same story share evidenceArtifactIds. The CR id is `CR-${epicHash}-${storyId}` (storage.ts:173). [files: .insrc/artifacts/CR-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s2.json, src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Older review stamps without reviewedBy, CRs without counts or with non-number counts, and findings stored in the ReviewReport shape are all read without throwing. The pass writes nothing.","evidence":"ReviewReport (review/types.ts:144-161) has reviewedBy optional ('Absent on reviews stamped before the field existed — read it through reviewerPartyOf'). code-review/gate.ts normalizeCounts (155-159) already reads non-number counts as 0, which the LLD mirrors. effectiveReviewVerdict reads f.severity on every finding, so the LLD's pre-filter of findings to well-formed entries is needed and specified. deriveGates is pure, with no store write. [files: src/workflow/review/types.ts, src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts, src/workflow/review/resolve.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"s3 stays inside sc5: it reads no stage (sc4) or currency (sc6) annotation, raises only its own notice codes, adds no items, and leaves joining needsAttention and the incomplete-evidence check to s5.","evidence":"The LLD postcondition says it 'reads no stage (sc4) or currency (sc6) annotation'. deriveStages is imported only in tests to assert ac2/ac5. The notices are limited to 'unplanned-task' and 'validation-conflict', which types.ts:120-121 marks '// s3'. The needsAttention join and incomplete-evidence are explicitly owned by s5 in the adjacent-scope list. deriveStages(graph, recordSet) exists at stage.ts:239 with that signature. [files: src/workflow/delivery/types.ts, src/workflow/delivery/stage.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every malformed input (non-object review, unknown verdict, malformed findings array or entries, malformed CR body/counts, malformed or unparseable task entries, dangling evidence ids) is detected with a stated, non-throwing response.","evidence":"Section 5 lists detection and response for each case. These match the real failure points. effectiveReviewVerdict throws on a null finding because it dereferences f.severity (resolve.ts:62), and the LLD filters findings first. taskIdToOrdinal and storyIdToOrdinal throw (id.ts:124,134), and the LLD wraps them. records/evidence lookups can miss, and the LLD skips those ids. Each case has an edge-case row and is covered by the 'malformed ... never throws' test. [files: src/workflow/review/resolve.ts, src/workflow/id.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of ac1–ac7 maps to at least one named gate.test.ts test over fixtures.ts, and the stage halves of ac2 and ac5 are asserted with deriveStages.","evidence":"The acceptance-mapping table covers ac1–ac7, each with named tests. ac2 and ac5 import deriveStages (stage.ts:239) to assert that the stage is unchanged. The fixtures module src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/fixtures.ts exists and already has the real-shape BUILD-0855311b6b32eb72-s1 record (line 150) used for the story-level conflict test. [files: src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/fixtures.ts, src/workflow/delivery/stage.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":14,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-08T12:01:03.608Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
